  body: "# Share fisherman in JSA and Income Support guidance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    definition combines work in the fishing industry, self-employment, specified boat or shore-based work
    and remuneration linked wholly or partly to the boat’s profits or gross earnings.\n\n## Scope and
    exceptions\n\nNot every fishing worker or piece-rate worker automatically meets the definition. The
    shore-based route has retirement or ill-health and continued-work conditions. DMG 27501 continues
    onto page 79 with an IS-specific British-boat qualification. JSA(Cont), JSA(IB) and IS earnings calculations
    differ; all additional conditions and current applicability remain unreviewed.\n\n## Inspected source
    passages\n\n- [DMG 27501, PDF page 78](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=78)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n- [DMG 27000, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f9e520b52e4144868939/dmg-Ch-27.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 27: Self-employed earners and share fishermen.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\n\
    Model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot.
    Specialist review is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this
    record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted
    text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage
    or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch27`: PDF SHA-256 `90b6c5ec739d2366936d67d78cd5a6f857b764b92000200f4a44ac956c88b3ac`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `7f84279f4a44373405ce06d32bf1c927a9f25dda507895b1540e6bb8b1b5185a`.\n"
