  - target: term/jsais-self-employed-earner
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Both branches of the share-fisherman definition explicitly require self-employment,
      alongside other conditions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch27/0078
      quote: "27501 A share fisherman is1\n\n\n1. a person who\n\n\n      1.1 usually works in the fishing
        industry and\n\n\n      1.2 is S/E and\n\n\n      1.3 is the master or a crew member of a fishing
        boat crewed by more than one person and\n\n\n      1.4 is paid for that work wholly or partly
        by a share of the profits or gross earnings of the fishing\n      boat or\n\n\n2. a person who\n\
        \n\n      2.1 was a person who worked as in 1., but has permanently stopped such work because
        of age or ill\n      health and\n\n\n      2.2 usually works\n\n\n            2.2.a ashore in
        GB (see DMG 070702) and\n\n\n            2.2.b as S/E and\n\n\n            2.2.c making or mending
        any gear belonging to a fishing boat or performing other services\n            that help, or are
        connected with, a fishing boat and\n\n\n      2.3 is paid for that work wholly or partly by a
        share of the profits or gross earnings of the fishing\n      boat and\n\n\n      2.4 has not ceased
        to usually work as described in 2.2."
      locator: DMG 27501
